WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.796 --> 00:00:17.540
the incident with Buttercup, Dan tried to behave for a few days.

2
00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:23.904
But it wasn't long before he went back to his old ways.

3
00:00:23.924 --> 00:00:28.528
"Let's have some fun," he said one night to Nat.

4
00:00:31.468 --> 00:00:36.290
He pulled a bottle of root beer, a small cake, and some cards from under his bed.

5
00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.311
Nat's eyes widened.

6
00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:41.952
"Where did you get that food?"

7
00:00:42.312 --> 00:00:42.873
he asked.

8
00:00:42.893 --> 00:00:48.035
"It was sitting in the kitchen all day," Dan explained with a shrug.

9
00:00:48.055 --> 00:00:52.317
"Asia always tells me I can help myself to snacks.

10
00:00:54.177 --> 00:00:56.678
Besides, nobody is around—Mr.

11
00:00:56.758 --> 00:00:58.399
Bauer's away, and Mrs.

12
00:00:58.479 --> 00:01:01.825
Bauer is busy with Teddy, who's sick or something.

13
00:01:02.825 --> 00:01:04.546
Don't you want to learn how to play poker?"

14
00:01:06.327 --> 00:01:09.268
Tempted by the adventure, Nat nodded.

15
00:01:09.288 --> 00:01:15.471
"Well, we need another player, so go get Tommy, and bring a candle for more light."

16
00:01:15.491 --> 00:01:20.373
"I'll bring Demi too," said Nat, who shared a room with Demi.

17
00:01:20.393 --> 00:01:24.735
"No, he'll just tell on us or try to stop us.

18
00:01:25.975 --> 00:01:27.696
Besides, he's probably asleep."

19
00:01:29.192 --> 00:01:34.556
Nat ran off and returned with a candle and Tommy, who was always ready for fun.

20
00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:42.402
"First we'll eat, and then we'll play cards for money," Dan said as he passed the root beer

21
00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:43.282
and cake around.

22
00:01:47.505 --> 00:01:48.626
what real men do."

23
00:01:48.646 --> 00:01:53.430
"I wish we didn't have to be so quiet," Tommy said softly.

24
00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:56.472
"But we don't want Silas to hear us."

25
00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:00.877
Silas managed the property for Mr.

26
00:02:00.917 --> 00:02:03.497
Bauer, and his room was right next door.

27
00:02:07.599 --> 00:02:12.620
Suddenly a voice in the hall wailed, "I can't find Nat!"

28
00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.481
Then the boys heard the patter of bare feet.

29
00:02:16.501 --> 00:02:20.802
"It's Demi, and he's gone to get Mrs.

30
00:02:20.902 --> 00:02:24.443
Bauer," Dan cried, whisking everything out of sight.

31
00:02:24.463 --> 00:02:26.804
"Get in bed, everyone!"

32
00:02:29.688 --> 00:02:31.689
Tommy and Nat flew to their rooms.

33
00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:38.352
Hearing Demi's voice again, Nat quickly blew out his candle and tossed it under his bed.

34
00:02:40.413 --> 00:02:45.335
When Demi arrived with Jo a few seconds later, Nat was pretending to be asleep.

35
00:02:46.815 --> 00:02:48.416
But Jo wasn't fooled.

36
00:02:48.436 --> 00:02:52.098
"What mischief are you up to?"

37
00:02:52.118 --> 00:02:57.460
"What?" Nat said sleepily.

38
00:02:58.876 --> 00:03:06.922
"I only ran into Dan's room for a minute I'm so sleepy Jo gave up and returned to

39
00:03:06.982 --> 00:03:09.783
Teddy, and Nat was soon asleep for real.

40
00:03:11.164 --> 00:03:16.808
Little did he realize what was happening under his bed—the candle was not out!

41
00:03:18.669 --> 00:03:22.412
Meanwhile Silas had awakened because he smelled something burning.

42
00:03:23.553 --> 00:03:28.316
Poking his head into the hall, he saw smoke coming from Nat and Demi's room.

43
00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:31.433
"Fire! Fire!"

44
00:03:31.813 --> 00:03:34.974
Silas cried, running to rescue the sleeping boys.

45
00:03:36.915 --> 00:03:40.596
Nat's bed was on fire, and the flames were licking the curtains.

46
00:03:42.177 --> 00:03:46.759
By the time Silas had pulled Nat and Demi to safety, Jo was on the scene.

47
00:03:46.779 --> 00:03:50.901
"Dan! Jack!

48
00:03:51.261 --> 00:03:52.561
Bring water from the bathroom!

49
00:03:53.782 --> 00:03:55.443
Tommy, get more buckets from the kitchen!

50
00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:58.304
Daisy, tell Asia I need her right now!

51
00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.841
Rob, stay out of the way!"

52
00:04:04.003 --> 00:04:05.964
The fire was quickly under control.

53
00:04:08.765 --> 00:04:13.968
Demi was more frightened than hurt, but Nat had a painful burn on his arm.

54
00:04:16.249 --> 00:04:16.730
When Mr.

55
00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.291
Bauer returned the next day, the boys gathered around him.

56
00:04:22.072 --> 00:04:29.569
Nat and Tommy immediately apologized for lying about the poker game, and the danger they'd caused, but Dan

57
00:04:29.649 --> 00:04:30.709
remained defiant.

58
00:04:30.729 --> 00:04:36.053
"You know I hate gambling, Dan," the professor said with a frown.

59
00:04:36.073 --> 00:04:39.755
"And you took a treat that Asia had left for Silas!

60
00:04:41.256 --> 00:04:44.419
Worst of all, you've involved the other boys in your misdeeds."

61
00:04:44.439 --> 00:04:48.641
"I didn't know it was a treat for Silas," Dan snapped.

62
00:04:48.662 --> 00:04:51.704
"Besides, not much harm was done."

63
00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:54.566
"Not much harm?"

64
00:04:55.326 --> 00:04:57.828
The professor raised his eyebrows in surprise.

65
00:04:59.092 --> 00:05:04.035
"The burn on Nat's arm is a terrible punishment, and Tommy is truly sorry.

66
00:05:04.135 --> 00:05:07.037
But you, Dan, have not even apologized.

67
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:14.361
We've forgiven you many times, but it has done no good—you're still setting a bad example.

68
00:05:15.862 --> 00:05:18.624
So say good-bye to everyone, and pack up your things."

69
00:05:20.665 --> 00:05:21.645
"Where's he going?"

70
00:05:21.966 --> 00:05:22.686
Nat cried.

71
00:05:22.706 --> 00:05:24.487
"To Mr.

72
00:05:24.507 --> 00:05:26.817
Page's school in the country because Mr.

73
00:05:26.857 --> 00:05:29.078
Page has straightened out many troubled boys."

74
00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:32.141
"Will he ever come back?"

75
00:05:32.441 --> 00:05:33.182
Demi asked.

76
00:05:33.202 --> 00:05:37.966
"I hope so, but that's up to Dan himself," Mr.

77
00:05:38.006 --> 00:05:38.767
Bauer said.

78
00:05:41.429 --> 00:05:42.009
After Mr.

79
00:05:42.049 --> 00:05:45.773
Bauer left the room, the boys were full of questions for Dan.

80
00:05:45.793 --> 00:05:48.275
"Will you like it at Mr.

81
00:05:48.335 --> 00:05:49.156
Page's school?"

82
00:05:49.536 --> 00:05:50.317
Jack asked.

83
00:05:50.337 --> 00:05:54.140
"I won't stay if I don't," Dan replied.

84
00:05:55.568 --> 00:05:56.469
"Where would you go?"

85
00:05:56.949 --> 00:05:57.770
Nat asked.

86
00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:04.496
"Maybe I'll go to sea or out to California," Dan said with a reckless air that startled the

87
00:06:04.536 --> 00:06:08.059
boys. "Oh, don't do that!

88
00:06:08.499 --> 00:06:09.080
Stay with Mr.

89
00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.902
Page awhile and then come back here," Nat pleaded.

90
00:06:11.922 --> 00:06:15.205
"I'm never coming back here!"

91
00:06:17.647 --> 00:06:22.050
Dan stormed upstairs to pack his things, every one of which Mr.

92
00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:23.512
Bauer had given him.

93
00:06:25.932 --> 00:06:32.657
When it was time to leave, Jo came outside, looking so sad that Dan felt remorseful.

94
00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:36.019
"May I go in to say good-bye to Teddy?"

95
00:06:36.279 --> 00:06:36.839
he asked.

96
00:06:36.859 --> 00:06:43.664
"Yes, he'll miss his Danny very much," Jo said, and followed him upstairs.

97
00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:52.430
While Dan was bending over Teddy's bed, he heard Jo talking to her husband.

98
00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:58.622
"Can't we give him another chance—he's the only boy we've ever failed with."

99
00:07:00.084 --> 00:07:00.584
But Mr.

100
00:07:00.624 --> 00:07:02.606
Bauer's mind was firmly made up.

101
00:07:04.087 --> 00:07:08.591
Dan wanted to ask for one more chance, but his pride wouldn't allow him.

102
00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:15.456
So, with a stony look on his face, he climbed into the wagon.

103
00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.521
A few days later, Mr.

104
00:07:21.581 --> 00:07:24.384
Page sent a letter, saying Dan was doing well.

105
00:07:25.984 --> 00:07:31.649
But three weeks later, another letter arrived, and this one said that Dan had run away.

106
00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:34.451
Mr. Bauer sighed.

107
00:07:34.471 --> 00:07:37.694
"Perhaps I should have given him another chance."

108
00:07:37.714 --> 00:07:41.557
"Don't worry, Fritz," Jo said.

109
00:07:41.577 --> 00:07:44.740
"I'm sure he'll come back to us."

110
00:07:46.481 --> 00:07:49.804
But time passed, and Dan did not return.
